+# Bulk link creation API
+
+Let partners create many short links in one call with independent per-item outcomes.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- **FR-1** POST /api/v1/links/bulk accepts between 1 and 100 link requests (url, optional customAlias, optional expiresAt).
+  - Acceptance: A request with 2 valid items returns HTTP 200 with created=2 and two results in request order.
+  - Acceptance: Each created item exposes the same fields as the single-create API (code, shortUrl, targetUrl, ...).
+- **FR-2** Items are processed independently; an invalid or conflicting item does not prevent other items from being created.
+  - Acceptance: An unsafe URL is reported as status=error with error.status=400 while valid siblings are created.
+  - Acceptance: A duplicate custom alias within the batch is reported with error.status=409.
+- **FR-3** Batches with zero items, more than 100 items, or no items field are rejected as a whole with HTTP 400.
+  - Acceptance: items: [] returns 400 with an RFC 9457 problem detail
+  - Acceptance: 101 items returns 400 and creates nothing
+
+## Design
+
+New BulkLinkController at POST /api/v1/links/bulk that loops over the items and delegates each one to the existing LinkService.create, translating domain exceptions into per-item error results.
+
+- D1: Reuse LinkService.create per item instead of a repository-level batch insert - Validation, alias reservation and SSRF rules stay in one place; no duplicated business logic.
+- D2: Each item runs in its own transaction (partial success) - Matches the requirement that items are independent; one bad URL must not roll back the others.
+- D3: Return HTTP 200 with per-item status instead of 207 Multi-Status - 207 is WebDAV-specific and poorly supported by client libraries; per-item status is explicit.
+- D4: Enforce 1..100 items with Bean Validation on the request DTO; do not cascade @Valid to items - Batch-level shape errors fail fast with 400; item-level errors must be reported per item.
+
+## API changes
+
+- POST /api/v1/links/bulk (new, additive)
+
+## Files changed
+
+- `src/main/java/io/agentic/shortener/web/BulkLinkController.java`
+- `src/main/java/io/agentic/shortener/web/dto/BulkCreateLinksRequest.java`
+- `src/main/java/io/agentic/shortener/web/dto/BulkCreateLinksResponse.java`
+- `src/test/java/io/agentic/shortener/web/BulkLinkApiIntegrationTest.java`
+
+## Limitations
+
+Generated from templates (LLM unavailable); review wording.
